{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WyVARkfPvSnoeNjWpmxxfo","type":"tool_result","content":"# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\n# Loop poll intervals. Unset loops keep their defaults (scanners 4h, triage\n# 15m, workers 5m, reviewers 5m, prwatch 5m); 1m is the minimum. The merger\n# is controller code with no agent or job slot, so a short interval costs only\n# GitHub API reads and gets reviewed PRs merged sooner.\nintervals: { merger: 1m }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make lint test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nThis adds owner-set priority labels (P0 to P3) that order candidates within each pool class and order the merger's queue. The design is already detailed and the work it was waiting on has landed: the slot wake-up change is on main (PR #403) and so is the CLAUDE.md invariant wording (PR #397). It goes to the engineer planner and then the engineer worker.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: turn the design into steps for the proposed two-part split (labels, pool ranking, loop wiring and the extra searches first; merger ordering and the starvation-warning fix second), building on the pool code as it now stands after the wake-up change, with the table tests the acceptance criteria list.\n- worker engineer: Go changes in internal/labels, internal/pool, the triage, worker, reviewer, scanner and merger loops, plus the proposal docs.\n\n## Open issues\n- The issue covers about 900 changed lines and proposes two PRs, the second depending on the first. A maintainer may want to file part 2 as its own issue so that each PR stays reviewable.\n- No product-manager, architect or documentation-planner triage roles exist here. The issue says those reviews were already folded into the design, so only the engineer plans it.\n- The CLAUDE.md wording is already on main, so the worker must not touch CLAUDE.md. It is a protected path.\npackage pool\n\nimport \"time\"\n\n// Candidate is one job a loop would like to start.\ntype Candidate struct {\n\tClass Class\n\t// Role is the role directory name, e.g. \"lead\", \"security-review\", \"cve\".\n\tRole string\n\t// Number is the issue (triage, worker) or PR (review) number, and 0 for\n\t// scanner runs. Negative numbers are allowed (dry-run synthetic issues).\n\tNumber int\n\t// Since is when the job became eligible; required. Triage and worker use\n\t// the issue's created_at, reviewers the PR's created_at, and a scanner run\n\t// the time it became due (last run plus interval).\n\tSince time.Time\n}\n\n// Key returns KeyFor(c.Class, c.Role, c.Number); callers never build keys by hand.\nfunc (c Candidate) Key() string { return KeyFor(c.Class, c.Role, c.Number) }\n\n// invalid returns the first rule the candidate breaks, or \"\".\nfunc (c Candidate) invalid() string {\n\tswitch {\n\tcase !c.Class.valid():\n\t\treturn \"unknown class \" + c.Class.String()\n\tcase c.Role == \"\":\n\t\treturn \"empty role\"\n\tcase c.Since.IsZero():\n\t\treturn \"zero Since\"\n\tcase c.Class == ClassScanner && c.Number != 0:\n\t\treturn \"scanner candidate must have number 0\"\n\tcase c.Class != ClassScanner && c.Number == 0:\n\t\treturn c.Class.String() + \" candidate must have a non-zero number\"\n\t}\n\treturn \"\"\n}\n\n// less is a total order on distinct keys: class, then oldest Since, then\n// lower Number, then Role. It does not depend on input order.\nfunc less(a, b Candidate) bool {\n\tif a.Class != b.Class {\n\t\treturn a.Class < b.Class\n\t}\n\tif !a.Since.Equal(b.Since) {\n\t\treturn a.Since.Before(b.Since)\n\t}\n\tif a.Number != b.Number {\n\t\treturn a.Number < b.Number\n\t}\n\treturn a.Role < b.Role\n}\n// Package pool arbitrates the shared pool of job slots (max_pods).\n//\n// Loops offer candidates once per tick; the pool decides which may start.\n// Nothing is queued: candidates are re-derived from GitHub every poll. The\n// pool does no I/O, so it sits outside the effect layer and behaves the same\n// under --dry-run. It imports only the standard library.\npackage pool\n\nimport \"fmt\"\n\n// Class is a job's priority class. Lower values fill first. The integer\n// values are persisted in state (jobs.priority): never reorder them.\ntype Class int\n\n// Priority classes, highest priority first.\nconst (\n\tClassReview  Class = iota // reviewers fill first\n\tClassWorker               // workers\n\tClassTriage               // triage\n\tClassScanner              // scanners fill last\n)\n\nvar classNames = [...]string{\"review\", \"worker\", \"triage\", \"scanner\"}\n\nfunc (c Class) valid() bool { return c >= ClassReview && c <= ClassScanner }\n\n// String returns \"review\", \"worker\", \"triage\" or \"scanner\", else \"class(N)\".\nfunc (c Class) String() string {\n\tif c.valid() {\n\t\treturn classNames[c]\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"class(%d)\", int(c))\n}\n\n// ParseClass is the inverse of String. The merger and the Reaper take no\n// slot, so they have no class and ParseClass rejects them.\nfunc ParseClass(s string) (Class, error) {\n\tfor i, n := range classNames {\n\t\tif n == s {\n\t\t\treturn Class(i), nil\ninternal/labels/labels.go:55:func Static() []string {\ninternal/labels/labels.go-56-\treturn []string{Pending, ExecutorFailed, NeedsHuman, NeedsApproval, Hold, Approved, TestsFailed, Keep, Pause}\ninternal/labels/labels.go-57-}\ninternal/labels/labels.go-58-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-59-// Name builds ard:<stage>:<role>[:<state>]. Request(StageTriage, \"lead\") is\ninternal/labels/labels.go-60-// the single special case and returns Pending. Names are not validated here:\ninternal/labels/labels.go-61-// callers pass roles that config has already validated, and Desired\ninternal/labels/labels.go-62-// validates the catalogue.\ninternal/labels/labels.go-63-func Name(s Stage, role string, st State) string {\ninternal/labels/labels.go-64-\tif s == StageTriage && role == \"lead\" && st == StateRequest {\ninternal/labels/labels.go-65-\t\treturn Pending\ninternal/labels/labels.go-66-\t}\ninternal/labels/labels.go-67-\tn := Prefix + string(s) + \":\" + role\ninternal/labels/labels.go-68-\tif st != StateRequest {\ninternal/labels/labels.go-69-\t\tn += \":\" + string(st)\ninternal/labels/labels.go-70-\t}\ninternal/labels/labels.go-71-\treturn n\ninternal/labels/labels.go-72-}\ninternal/labels/labels.go-73-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-74-// Request is the label that asks a role to run.\ninternal/labels/labels.go-75-func Request(s Stage, role string) string { return Name(s, role, StateRequest) }\ninternal/labels/labels.go-76-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-77-// Running marks a claim.\ninternal/labels/labels.go-78-func Running(s Stage, role string) string { return Name(s, role, StateRunning) }\ninternal/labels/labels.go-79-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-80-// Done marks completion.\ninternal/labels/labels.go-81-func Done(s Stage, role string) string { return Name(s, role, StateDone) }\ninternal/labels/labels.go-82-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-83-// Changes is a reviewer's request-changes verdict.\ninternal/labels/labels.go-84-func Changes(role string) string { return Name(StageReview, role, StateChanges) }\ninternal/labels/labels.go-85-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-86-// Scanner is the label a scanner puts on the issues it files.\ninternal/labels/labels.go-87-func Scanner(name string) string { return Prefix + \"scanner:\" + name }\ninternal/labels/labels.go-88-\ninternal/labels/labels.go-89-// CheckIntake reports whether name may be the intake label (config\ninternal/labels/labels.go-90-// intake.label). It rejects any name Parse accepts, that is any static label\ninternal/labels/labels.go-91-// and any ard:<stage>:<role>[:<state>] or ard:scanner:<name>, except\ninternal/labels/labels.go-92-// ard:pending (the default intake label, matched case-insensitively). \"\"\ninternal/labels/labels.go-93-// means the default and is accepted. It checks nothing else: config already\ninternal/labels/labels.go-94-// enforces the ard: prefix, length and characters. This is the one copy of\ninternal/labels/labels.go-95-// the rule. intake.Admit, Desired and `ard config check` all call it.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d481f9e4-65f1-47d6-a6fa-143d5adb3ac5","uuid":"10182805-b0bb-4c45-9fc4-e5f8417eb097","timestamp":"2026-11-25T13:08:59.093Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard ser